# React and TypeScript

- Vite, React, and TypeScript with `strict`. Do not use `any`.
- Function components and hooks only.
- Keep server state in TanStack Query. Keep UI state in the component or the URL.
- One component per file. Reusable logic goes in a `useX` hook.
- Pass props explicitly. Use context only for something truly global.
- Data screens render loading, empty, and error states.

```tsx
// Good: the query owns the request, the component owns the states
const studies = useStudies(filters);

if (studies.isPending) return <p>Loading studies…</p>;
if (studies.isError) return <p role="alert">The study list could not be loaded.</p>;
if (studies.data.length === 0) return <p>No studies match these filters.</p>;
```

- Use native buttons, labels on fields, visible focus, and semantic HTML.
- Colocate styles in a CSS Module. Do not add a new global stylesheet per component.
